{
  "doc": [
    "Memories stream (docs/mesh-design.md §3, lot P0). Reference: src/vault/contracts.ts. Schema of the plaintext payloads: memory-event.schema.json.",
    "Stream: memory events travel as ordinary sealed vault events (header {v, user_id, conversation_id, event_id, epoch, kind, created_at}, XChaCha20-Poly1305 under HKDF-SHA256(epoch key, salt 'twoody/vault/conversation/v1', info conversation_id, 32), header canonical bytes as AAD — exactly sealEvent/openEvent of twoody-desktop src/shared/vault.ts) with kind 'memory' or 'tombstone' in their own stream (backend vault_events.stream = 'memories'). conversation_id = memories stream id; the payload is the JSON of the event (UTF-8).",
    "Stream id: uuid5-shaped (uuidFrom of vaultSync.ts: first 16 bytes, byte 6 = (b & 0x0f) | 0x50, byte 8 = (b & 0x3f) | 0x80, 8-4-4-4-12 lowercase hex) of HKDF-SHA256(ikm = the epoch-1 key, salt = UTF-8 'twoody/vault/memories-id/v1', info = empty, length 16). Epoch 1 is used whatever the current epoch, so the id never changes; the events themselves are sealed under the current epoch as usual.",
    "Content hash: normalise = String.toLowerCase() (no locale) → NFKD → remove every \\p{M} → replace each run of characters not in \\p{L} or \\p{N} by one ASCII space → trim spaces; content_hash = lowercase hex SHA-256 of its UTF-8. Empty after normalising → no hash, never learned. Local source 'conversation' (memoryLearning.ts) maps to 'learned'.",
    "Learned memory id: uuidFrom(HMAC-SHA256(key = HKDF-SHA256(epoch-1 key, salt 'twoody/vault/memories-id/v1', info 'learned', 32), msg = UTF-8 of content_hash hex)). Keyed so the account cannot confirm a guessed fact. Manual and imported memories take a random UUID v4.",
    "Event ids (the header's event_id, unique per account): eventIdFor(stream_id, kind, ref) of twoody-desktop vaultSync.ts = uuidFrom(SHA-256('twoody/vault/event-id/v1\\n' + stream_id + '\\n' + kind + '\\n' + ref)) with ref = 'learned\\n' + id for a learned event (the same wherever the fact is learned: the account keeps it once), id + '\\n' + hlc + '\\n' + device for a manual/import memory event, id + '\\n' + hlc for a tombstone (kind 'tombstone'). A person editing a learned memory writes a 'manual' event.",
    "HLC: '<wall>-<counter>', wall = Unix ms zero-padded to 13 digits, counter 0..9999 zero-padded to 4; string order = clock order. tick(last, now): wall = max(last.wall, now), counter = last.counter + 1 if wall = last.wall else 0. receive(last, remote, now): if remote.wall > now + 3600000 the remote clock is not adopted (= tick); else wall = max(last.wall, remote.wall, now), counter = max of the counters of those equal to wall, + 1 (0 when only now). A counter past 9999 carries: wall + 1, counter 0. device = the writer's vault device id.",
    "Merge (commutative, idempotent): drop payloads that do not match the schema ('invalid') and learned events whose id is not the learned id of their content ('learned_id_mismatch'); one event per event_id (two different copies: the lesser by the order below). Per memory id the winner is the greatest by: hlc; then tombstone > memory; then source manual > import > learned; then device id (string order); then event_id. Forbidden hashes F = content hashes of every memory event of every id whose winner is a tombstone; learned events whose hash is in F are left out ('forbidden_hash') and winners recomputed until F stops growing. Result: memories = winners that are memory events, minus learned ones whose hash equals a live manual/import memory's (hidden_duplicates); tombstoned = ids whose winner is a tombstone. Superseded memories stay in the set. All lists sorted by id / event_id (string order).",
    "sealed_memory_event: the first scenario's memory sealed under epoch 1 with a fixed nonce; it opens with openEvent of twoody-desktop and twoody-app unchanged."
  ],
